WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Ukraine's targeted strikes on Russian oil refineries threaten energy flows that millions across Europe depend on for fuel and power. This is Omni View, episode 135. Ukrainian forces hit two Russian oil refineries in coordinated strikes. President Zelensky stated the military carried out the attacks as part of efforts to weaken Russia's war economy. Russian forces continued strikes on Ukrainian cities in the same period. Lithuania's defense minister

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:56.720
Robertus Countess warned that Russia could be considering possible false flag provocations against NATO countries in the Baltic region. Countess said there was no specific date for any potential Russian actions, but authorities were monitoring Russia's plans and exchanging information with Poland and other NATO allies. The Guardian reported the refinery hits as a direct response to sustained Russian bombardment of Ukrainian urban areas.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:17.820
Lithuanian defense minister Robertus Countess warned that Russia might stage false flag incidents near NATO borders and said Baltic states were sharing intelligence with Poland and other allies to monitor developments. Ukrainian officials framed the refinery strikes as necessary pressure on Russia's ability to fund its military campaign.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:37.440
Russian statements reflected in regional coverage present Ukrainian actions as escalation that endangers civilian energy supplies. The strikes occurred against a backdrop of continued Russian attacks on Ukrainian cities, with both sides exchanging blows that affect energy infrastructure on each side of the border.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:56.100
What happens next? The first compliance deadlines land in six months, and regulators say the earliest enforcement cases will show how strictly the rules bite, shifting now to Sudan. More than 200 pyramids at the marrow site face damage from Sudan's ongoing war and lack of protection.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:11.440
The location holds UNESCO World Heritage Status, fighting and neglect have left the structures exposed. Combat near the site and the withdrawal of conservation teams have increased the risk of irreversible harm to the sandstone monuments.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:18.780
Al Jazeera documented the physical risks to the pyramids from nearby combat and abandoned conservation work.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:35.980
Sudanese authorities have limited capacity to secure remote heritage sites while resources focus on immediate security needs. International heritage groups note that similar conflicts elsewhere have led to irreversible losses when sites remain unguarded for extended periods.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:44.820
The combination of active fighting and reduced maintenance has created conditions where even minor incidents could accelerate deterioration of the structures.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:03:03.620
Next, an Ebola outbreak in Congo, Kinchasa. Child deaths from Ebola have passed 300 in the current outbreak. UNICEF reports that fear and service disruption have cut childhood immunizations, safe deliveries, and other essential care by more than 40% in the hardest hit areas.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:17.880
Local health workers must divide attention between treating Ebola cases and sustaining regular medical services. The drop in routine care raises the prospect of secondary outbreaks of diseases that vaccines normally prevent.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:32.100
All Africa coverage highlights how local health workers are stretched between outbreak response and maintaining regular services. UNICEF emphasizes that reduced routine care risks secondary outbreaks of preventable diseases.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:48.620
Health officials in the region state that restoring trust in clinics remains a central challenge while transmission continues. The decline in safe deliveries and immunization stems directly from both facility closures and community avoidance of health centers during the outbreak.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:04:02.280
Meanwhile, China has opened an investigation into the U.S. Cybersecurity firm Palo Alto Networks. Beijing's cyberspace administration launched a review of products sold in China by the U.S. firm.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.960
The stated goal is to protect critical infrastructure and reduce cybersecurity risks.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:20.960
The administration said the review was being conducted to ensure the secure and stable operation of critical information infrastructure, prevent cybersecurity risks and vulnerabilities, and safeguard national security.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:33.020
The probe follows recent U.S. restrictions on Chinese technology companies. The South China Morning Post reported the probe follows recent U.S. restrictions on Chinese technology.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:45.600
Chinese regulators described the step as a standard security check applied to foreign suppliers. U.S. industry observers see it as part of broader reciprocal measures in the technology sector.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:56.060
The investigation targets products already installed in Chinese networks and examines whether they introduce vulnerabilities into systems that support essential services.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:09.380
Turning to the economy, SpaceX posted a 92% revenue increase in its first post-IPO results. The company reported a sharp rise in revenue for the period after its public listing.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:22.740
Growth came mainly from launch contracts and satellite services. Early engineer Andre Lavois, who joined in 2009, described plans to sell portions of his shares now that the company is publicly traded.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:28.080
The results reflect sustained demand across both commercial and government customers.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:34.000
Niche Asia noted the results reflect continued demand for commercial and government launches.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:40.980
Investors have focused on whether the post-IPO structure changes capital allocation for future projects.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:48.580
A BBC profile of an early engineer highlighted individual shareholders now able to sell portions of their holdings.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:56.980
The revenue jump occurred even as the company manages expanded operations across multiple launch sites and satellite constellations.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:06:07.040
In Germany, factory orders rose despite higher input costs. Orders unexpectedly increased in June as companies built stockpiles of parts and equipment.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:18.540
Demand held steady even as material costs climbed. Businesses appear to be accumulating inventory to guard against possible supply interruptions linked to tensions in the Middle East.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:24.780
The June increase occurred while input costs rose sharply across several manufacturing sectors.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:31.740
The Wall Street Journal linked the resilience to concerns over potential supply interruptions from Middle East tensions.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:36.600
Manufacturers appear to be front loading purchases to avoid future shortages.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:45.340
Economist note that such stockpiling can support output in the short term but may mask underlying weakness if new orders later slow.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:51.680
The pattern suggests companies are prioritizing continuity of production over immediate cost control.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:59.540
Now, some progress worth knowing about. Takeda seeks inclusion of its dengue vaccine in India's national program.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:05.560
The company is working to add its dengue vaccine to India's childhood immunization schedule.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:11.780
Officials aim to expand protection against the disease that affects large parts of the country each year.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:16.600
The effort follows successful trials and regulatory reviews in other markets.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:22.940
Indian health authorities are evaluating cost and supply capacity before any rollout decision.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:28.520
Nikkeh Asia reported the effort follows successful trials and regulatory reviews.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:35.540
The main complication remains aligning vaccine pricing and distribution logistics with existing program budgets.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:43.300
The company must demonstrate that the vaccine can be produced and delivered at scale within India's public health infrastructure.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:48.840
Now, to really understand this story, there is something most coverage leaves out.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.260
Most reporting on strikes against oil facilities focuses on immediate damage counts.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:04.680
Yet the deeper mechanism is how such attacks shift global refining capacity and force buyers to reroute crude and product flows over weeks or months.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:16.580
When a refinery goes offline, nearby plants must increase runs or imports must rise, raising costs for every downstream user from trucking fleets to power generators.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:31.320
Historical cases such as disruptions during the 2019 attacks on Saudi facilities showed that even partial shutdowns can lift regional product prices for 30 to 60 days until spare capacity elsewhere compensates.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:35.960
The same logic applies when Ukrainian strikes reduce Russian output.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:43.480
European buyers may turn to alternative suppliers, lengthening shipping routes and tightening available tanker capacity.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:57.700
Knowing this pattern, when coverage highlights a single day strike, readers can check whether follow-up reporting tracks actual throughput data from neighboring refineries or changes in tanker bookings rather than stopping at the initial explosion.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:08.040
The concrete detail to verify next is whether official monthly oil product export figures from the affected countries show a sustained drop or a quick rebound.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:15.560
If you want to go deeper on the Ukraine refinery strikes, compare how the Guardian and Nikkei Asia are covering it.

